(10. Periodic updation of KYC. KYC must be updated at least once every two years for high-risk) Tj T*
(customers, once every eight years for medium-risk customers and once every ten years for low-) Tj T*
(risk customers. Customers must receive at least three reminders before the due date. If KYC is) Tj T*
(not updated within 30 days of the due date, the account may be partially frozen.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(11. Record retention. KYC records and identification documents must be preserved for at least) Tj T*
(five years after the business relationship with the customer has ended or the account has been) Tj T*
(closed, whichever is later. Records of transactions must be preserved for at least five years) Tj T*
(from the date of the transaction. Records must not be destroyed earlier and must be made) Tj T*
(available to competent authorities on request.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
